  "why": [
    "Goal coverage used to match GOAL_REQUIREMENTS strings directly against registry strings.",
    "Those were different vocabularies: the requirement side said READ_INTEL_LIST / SELECT_INTEL /",
    "EXECUTE_INTEL while the registry said OPEN_INTEL / SELECT_INTEL_BEAST_MISSION /",
    "INTEL_BEAST_START_MARCH / DISPATCH_INTEL_BEAST. The mismatch made real capabilities look",
    "missing and made unbuilt requirements look satisfied. Coverage is therefore computed over a",
    "canonical capability layer: a goal needs capabilities, a capability is satisfied by one or",
    "more registered skills, and only the episode stream decides whether it is live-verified.",
    "",
    "This file is the INPUT mapping. The machine-readable coverage REPORT is written to",
    "knowledge/goals/capability_skill_map.json by tools/build_capability_coverage.py."
  ],
